{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread","id":290174,"title":"Bitching About ST Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-22T18:01:29-07:00","id":290174,"title":"Bitching About ST Thread","content":"There was a thread about this in the last forum that seemed pretty popular, so I figured let's revive it! It gives players a chance to bitch about their current or past STs, and STs can read it to see mistakes to avoid.<br /> <br /> I'll open with a story about a guy who used to run reasonably often in my first gaming group. This guy was a real 40k enthusiast: the kind that owns every edition of every codex of every race, drops a significant amount of his paycheck on the game, and has optimised his army to the degree of being unbeatable unless you were spending as much time or money on it as he was. These qualities would normally just be an annoying personality quirk, except they carried over to his game-running style. There was one way to progress in his games, and if you did not take it, you'd spend a lot of time sitting there and scratching your head. It was almost always the least interesting pathway.<br /> <br /> This was exemplified in a 3.5 D&amp;D game he ran. A sort-of sequel to a game he ran years ago with different people, it was essentially Lost World: adventurers are on an island full of dinosaurs. Sounds good, right? Right from the outset, he began to strip away the fun. We can <i>only</i> play Good characters, not even Neutral. We <i>cannot</i> play paladins. We <i>must</i> start with the listed sample gear for our class, regardless of our skills (which meant my ranger with points in Craft(Fletching) had no tools with which to make arrows). One player, new to D&amp;D and thought a barbarian would be fun, wanted to buy a parrot, since we were going on a ship, which made him want to be a pirate. Reasonable enough, he had some points in Animal Handling, so any ST wouldn't mind. After spending twenty minutes going through the PHB and DMG trying to find a standard price for a parrot, he set the price at 50gp, which for a starting character is totally unachievable, even if we all pooled our money together. Being a not-especially-clever barbarian, he drew his axe, intending to go for an intimidating (but not directly harming) strategy. Ok, kind of stupid, granted. The shopkeeper immediately started screaming for the guards, who were all fifth-level fighters. The barbarian only survived by obvious DM enforcement. So we get onto the ship, and spend the next two hours of game time trying to find a place on the ship that's out of the way. Apparently this is impossible on a ship designed to take passengers on longish voyages. Then pirates attacked, seemingly out of nowhere, and our characters somehow didn't notice until it was right on top of us. Again, we nearly died, only living through DM enforcement. Then we get to a town, a seedy place by all accounts. Our Good characters, noticing that the one clean source of water was being controlled by a group of rough halflings who charged exorbitant prices, wanted to stop this. The halflings were extremely aggressive third-level monks with 16 strength, dexterity and constitution. Again, we nearly died.<br /> <br /> I won't bother boring you with more details, but this continued, in fact got <i>worse</i>, all game. At no point did we affect things one iota, and the one time two of our characters <i>tried</i> by trying to nurse an injured Deinonychus back to health (with the intention of it being my rangers animal companion), he threw a T-Rex at us. A T-Rex that apparently killing us, even with us doing a surprising amount of damage to it, decided we were less effort than any of the easier and larger prey around. Then Greater Wyrm dragons got involved, and we were even more pointless.<br /> <br /> Well, how about you? Any STs, current or past, you want to bitch about?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T06:56:34-07:00","id":290477,"title":"","content":"I used to play D&amp;D with an DM who basically set up every &quot;adventure&quot; to be a thin justification for an <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/InterestingSituationDuel\" target=\"_blank\">Interesting Situation Duel</a> with some boss monster or collection of monsters he had designed. These fights usually took hours, and consisted mostly of us gradually whittling away at their health with weak attacks because he would contrive to deny us the use of our most powerful attacks. It got boring pretty fast.<br /> <br /> He also made a bunch of GMPCs that were essentially Super Smash Brothers characters. They didn't steal the spotlight, but it was annoying having them around because we didn't have a big enough party without them and also couldn't use them to any great advantage.<br /> <br /> To be fair, we were all epic-level characters who had the ability to deal damage in the hundreds. For us, pretty much all fights were binary - ridiculously easy, or ridiculously hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 10-23-2014, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T07:41:19-07:00","id":290487,"title":"","content":"Biggest gripe I ever had with an ST was in a LARP where he let his girlfriend have a bunch of extra points at character creation, so she was a 7th gen Toreador right out of the gate. After they broke up, it turned ugly for her. I set her up as the prime suspect in my character's destruction and other people in the game (who didn't like her either) smelled the blood in the water and got her Diableriezed WITH THE PRINCE'S SANCTION by the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Besides that, not had a lot of complaints, but I've also spent a lot of time AS the ST, so it's a little different for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T08:51:32-07:00","id":290529,"title":"","content":"An ST of mine has this annoying tendency to do his NPC's on the fly. This is good for him but he is a min-max type player. So he makes his NPC's have the exact perfect combination of abilities to do enough damage to us to almost kill us every time. And I say almost kill us because he has another tendency that irks me. Namely, he keeps track of our health so he can take us down to ALMOST dead but never kills us. I do not mind having my characters die, but he refuses to kill us.<br /> Another ST of mine thought I was sleeping with his wife. So he went out of his way to try to kill me every chance he could. It forced me to minmax all of my characters just to make sure that I could survive. And for the record? No, I was not sleeping with his wife. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T08:55:35-07:00","id":290530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=290529#post290529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another ST of mine thought I was sleeping with his wife. So he went out of his way to try to kill me every chance he could.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an extremely passive-aggressive response to adultery, real or imagined. Why did you keep playing with that guy, and why did he keep playing with you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 10-23-2014, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T08:58:32-07:00","id":290533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=290530#post290530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is an extremely passive-aggressive response to adultery, real or imagined. Why did you keep playing with that guy?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He was the only guy who knew how to run games. Plus, his wife was a good friend of mine who kept assuring me that he was &quot;not going to be a dick this time&quot; and I trusted her. Eventually, things came to a head and we all parted ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-23T09:01:22-07:00","id":290535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=290487#post290487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> ... not had a lot of complaints, but I've also spent a lot of time AS the ST, so it's a little different for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here. Most of the time, really, when I'm well enough to do the job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T04:26:00-07:00","id":291186,"title":"","content":"My ST last time dozed off during Roll20 and left for an hour, because he does not have balls to refuse his family.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-24T05:44:08-07:00","id":291214,"title":"","content":"I've had all of the STs you folks describe above except for the one thinking a player and his wife were fooling around (though I did have a player that had a similar kind of idea that I was trying to fool around with his girlfriend, which I thought was really strange since I introduced him to her because her and I were friends and I thought she'd like him).<br /> <br /> The two that I have the most complaints about are the one that confessed to me that he would intentionally make his campaigns as boring as possible so that the players would lose interest, and so that I would DM something again, because he'd rather play than DM even if it meant the DM he was playing for was pissed off at him for refusing him a chance to play for once (he didn't last long in my group after making that confession to me).<br /> <br /> The other is a fella that would do the nonsensical thing of granting all kinds of boosts to the player characters, and then giving even more of a boost to all the NPCs that were inevitably faced in combat - I'm cool with adjusting the difficulty of the game, but to fiddle with both sides of the PC vs. NPC equation is a sign of lacking intelligence because the same effect can be achieved with less work by only adjusting one side to a lesser degree - and would run his campaign such that the summary of each would be &quot;The party pissed off someone or something powerful that is now going to kill them if they don't kill it first&quot; and would send one nearly impossible fight after another at the party until he reached his end goal of killing of all the characters at once, or getting the players to quit playing.<br /> <br /> ...and then after no one wanted to play in any of his campaigns any more, and we all took a 3 year break from even having him in our games, we gave him another shot to play with us and he mentioned interest in running a campaign, to which we all told him we'd give him a shot if he promised it wouldn't be like those old campaigns that we all hated. This fool of an ST had the audacity to make the claim that his old campaigns were great, and that we thought so too - because, according to him, &quot;any campaign you remember years later is a good one.&quot;<br /> <br /> And he didn't believe us that it matters whether the memories are <i>good</i>, not just that we have them, even with a player incredulously shouting &quot;So what you are saying is that getting stabbed three times and robbed is a great lot of fun? You'll remember it your whole life, must be the best thing in the world!&quot;<br /> <br /> No surprise, really, but he didn't last long in our group on his second chance... and I'm not giving him a third.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Not so noble anymore.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1823-drake","name":"Drake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1823_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"456"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-25T22:38:05-07:00","id":292727,"title":"","content":"Jeez, where to begin...each of these entires is about a different GM. Despite them I have actually had some great GMs haha.<br /> <br /> (1) My first real D&amp;D DM was also a player's brother (specifically, the brother of the player who owned the house we played at in college). This guy...reminds me a lot of Allan53's DM. This was when Eberron first came out and it was so different in theme compared to either the Grayhawk or FR material we had seen that we definitely wanted to try it. Pretty much all of my problems with him stem from his attempts to run Eberron.<br /> -It seemed like no game he ran lasted more than a month or so, despite the DM's sister claiming he had been a great DM in the past. So, gen characters, run for a couple weeks, inevitably TPK or something because he totally sucked at balancing the encounter, repeat.<br /> -He decided we should all run multiple characters simultaneously, to have a bigger party and play with the system more. Of course this resulted in nearly every character being pretty one-dimensional: characterizing one character per person is a process. Having 2 or even 3 characters per person means each is little more than a character sheet with no personality.<br /> -It was alleged that he was secretly flirting with my other friend's girlfriend (both were players). The veracity of this is debated because said girlfriend was later proven to be a complete pathological liar. In any case, she was one of those obnoxious players who passed secret notes to the GM about her character. She claimed all her notes were game-related to her characters' obnoxious secret goals but that all of his responses were creepy shit.<br /> -He railroaded like none other and insisted on playing Eberron like Shadowrun (though I doubt he ever played Shadowrun). Like, insisted that we start at level 3 or so all the time. We get some mission to deliver a package to someone, in mid-mission we get ambushed by a part of 10 dwarf Frenzied Berserkers, all at least level 10. Now we resolved this narratively without combat (because combat would have been pointless) but we were definitely railroaded into his &quot;plots&quot; (I use the term loosely) by too-powerful-to-defeat NPCs. I think in the end I just started making excuses based on classwork and stopped showing up.<br /> <br /> (2) I had finished playing a completely successful chat-based L5R 4th edition campaign and was <i>super </i>into L5R at the time (still kinda am actually!). Got invited to join a slightly-in-progress L5R game with some people including people I had gamed with in the D&amp;D campaigns described above (different GM though). This GM was really knowledgeable about the L5R setting, having played the CCG for like 10 years, but basically did not ask anyone else in the group to bother learning the setting or its customs. For anyone familiar with L5R, part of the reason of playing is immersing in a setting following idealized Bushido rules, and how your duty and honor intersect with dishonorable things like personal ambition and lust, and resolving those issues. So basically if you don't bother to learn the setting and code of honor, you're really not playing true to the setting.<br /> -The GM didn't bother to educate players; a couple of them picked it up themselves and did absolutely great. Another played a shugenja (basically spellcasting priest of natural spirits) of a powerful but largely pacifist clan, as a D&amp;D evoker murderhobo, which is so far from the in-setting portrayal of that clan and role as I've ever seen.<br /> -The GM, I guess not wanting to leave people out, invited like 9 people to play the game in like 9-hour live sessions. Nuff said there imo.<br /> -A metric fuck-ton of metagaming was allowed to occur. Broke immersion sooooooo much.<br /> -I was the only person who opted to play a courtier (basically a social/face whose school powers revolve around the social interaction system). Moreso, the GM asked me to play this kind of character because nobody else had. Everyone else played some kind of bushi (warriors; there are a lot of different schools that offer different techniques) and there were also 2 shugenja. So a lot of the game revolved around combat plots and intrigue and pacifist priests throwing fireballs because they didn't care about the setting. Every week the GM kept promising me that court/social stuff would happen soon so I could actually <i>do something with effectiveness </i>(though I built such that I was a decent archer at least), but every session it was almost like monster-of-the-week. Eventually most of the bushi engaged in a TPK fight and the game ended. I never once got a truly social scene.<br /> <br /> (3) One guy I still play with IRL (former roommate) actually IS a great GM but just cannot run a game in a provided setting to save his life. He gets super-obsessive with home brewing the settings, which can be very creative but it just gets very overboard and the world-building takes on an unseemly interactive life of its own. Like, sometimes I just want to play in a setting I can read up on and understand, not dive into a modified setting from someone's head. This <i>always</i> gets super overwrought with like everyone expected to chime in with ways the setting has changed and I find this very off-putting since I feel like the GM is trying to shift the burden of world-building from himself (which he is already willingly taking on instead of using default D&amp;D, L5R or Exalted settings) to the players, and when I feel imposed on to generate content on demand like that I tend to get disillusioned and bored with the game pretty quick.<br /> <br /> (4) I went through a couple years where a LOT of my gaming involved playing Adeptus Evangelion by play-by-post (PbP). For those not in the know, AdEva is basically a rules hack to run Evangelion on the Dark Heresy 1e rule set. Some of the people I played with were great. Eventually I ended up with one GM who disclosed to us that he was 16 (most of the players were in their early to mid 20s). We were pretty ok with this, because the GM seemed pretty mature and stuff, and was a good writer, etc. In the end, man, this guy was THE ABSOLUTE WORST and I regret not immediately dropping when I heard he was 16. Nevertheless I continued on and get to experience some of these gems...<br /> -He started his games in a PbP format but asked us to sign into Skype to talk OOC more quickly. Sure, ok. Then he basically asked if we could do extra scenes on Skype text chat that would get posted to the forum. Sure, ok. Then the PbP stuff basically disappeared, he demanded we always play by chat, he was rude and dismissive if we were late or couldn't make it, etc.<br /> -I played in a 2-person game where both of us had extensive backstories. This game eventually wound up ending for a variety of reasons, but the GM decided to tell us how it was going to end had we played it out. The GM's Big Reveal was that our backstories were total lies, fabrications programmed into us or which our brains rationalized from stories we had heard or suggestions that had been planted. Basically he completely obviated our characters' pre-pilot lives utterly by saying we had been grown as Angel Hybrids. Such a possibility wasn't discussed, so it came across as a huge middle finger to our own visions for our characters and their self-determination.<br /> -GM basically had an Angel fuse with an Eva and literally described it as penetrative rape which the pilot felt through biofeedback. Having such content as a part of the game was not discussed in advance. He didn't see a problem until basically EVERY player complained about it, and even then reluctantly retconned it but never apologized for it.<br /> -The above issues, particularly scheduling issues, were a huge source of conflict between a bunch of people working real jobs and a 16-year-old who apparently was largely taking high school courses from his home computer. Basically the complaints about how horrible we were for not always being available to join impromptu scenes culminated in him entering into a long private message rant following a solo scene, basically &quot;justifying&quot; my character's horrible IC treatment and abuse at the hands of much more well-connected NPCs (which was VERY personal because of his issues with me &quot;not committing&quot; to his games enough). At this point I opted to leave the game and not continue playing, blocked him, and basically all other players followed suit. The result was this GM writing up like a 10-page long &quot;conclusory post&quot; for the game describing the Third Impact for this game, resulting in every player's grisly death at the hands of one horrifying Angel ultimate killed and eaten by one that was even worse. My character, playing the Ops Director (think Misato) actually died offscreen like an extra when the base exploded, which I personally found hilarious because I am SURE this GM considered it the ultimate &quot;fuck you&quot; to me.<br /> -This GM claimed that during the course of running his AdEva games (I didn't participate in all of them) that he had tried to commit suicide at least twice (once by trying to overdose on psych meds, once by jumping out of his window which resulted in some broken bones). And then was manipulative to get us to feel bad for him and his problems, while basically blaming us/the games he was running for the stress driving him to do this. Me, I think a really psychologically screwed up teen has no business getting so involved in the kind of themes related to Evangelion.<br /> <br /> (5) Most recently, a guy I have played with a couple times who always starts games and just....lets em die. Hypes his game like crazy, gets everyone excited, creates a dynamic world with a lot of plot hooks and then just kind of...drops the ball and goes off-grid. Once he basically said &quot;yeah you guys are doing such different things than I planned/approached the problem so sideways for that I'm really stumped&quot; and that was kind of it. Like, he didn't even try to figure it out, which just made everyone think we were on rails the whole time.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo...yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 10-27-2014, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T04:13:53-08:00","id":302020,"title":"","content":"Phew.. None of the above seem to be speaking about me!<br /> <br /> Anyway, when I first starting playing a WoD game it was VtM. I got introduced in a fairly abrupt way..<br /> I asked the ST, a friend of mine, what he was doing that night, and one hour later I had a character sheet and was sitting at a table ready to play a game I didn't know existed.<br /> <br /> But all went well, I started off silently and read up on rules asap. The campaign was alot of fun, until.... the ST introduced his own former character.<br /> This character was overpowered compared to the players and had some stuff I don't think is any of the rulebooks... Long story short, if we didn't follow this 'NPC' we wouldn't get any adventure. And if we did follow this 'NPC' he cleared up all the mess before we even knew what was going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4167-comedicus","name":"Comedicus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4167_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:15:58-08:00","id":302209,"title":"","content":"Well, there's a story I've told a couple times on RPG.net that has always been my gold standard for truly horrible storytelling, but I don't know if it ever talked about it on any iteration of these forums. I'll cut it down to the short version: The ST of a VtM game had a good thing going, with several players having by all accounts a great time. One-by-one he compelled the characters to do counter-intuitive, stupid things that made them vanish, collected our sheets, redid them by hand as powered-down members of his homebrew angel/demon/vampire hybrid bloodline, and then physically tore up the old ones in small pieces in front of us and threw them in the trash before we could compare what we had before to what we had now. <br /> The game may have lasted two sessions after, with a meek, apologetic, &quot;You guys can have your old characters back&quot; as too little, too late.<br /> <br /> There was also the ST who got skeevy and maybe a little oversexed at a mixed table WtA, where comfort levels had not been previously discussed. Shortly thereafter, the game came to a halt; he's tried to propose getting things going again, but only one of the players is even roughly amenable to the idea; one has dropped off the face of the planet, but two of them are explicitly too uncomfortable with the way he was going, and the other just doesn't enjoy his style of GMing (pat self on the back a lot any time you feel like you've surprised players, and constantly grin and speak loudly because it makes players think what you just said was cool). He did the same things later at a Dragonstar game, informing one character who had been transferred into a wholly mechanical body that his new form was anatomically correct and &quot;wired for pleasure&quot;, and let another, turned part-satyr via an ambiguously-worded <i>wish</i> spell, know that she was now constantly turned on and having her constantly propositioned until she was pregnant. He just grinned wildly when asked about it and said &quot;Oh, when I realized what had happened I had to do it!&quot;<br /> <br /> There was also the guy who ran a one-shot game of Exalted at a con, who didn't really think much about the mechanical ramifications of the half-dozen rule hacks he put in place for his friends who were oWoD players (I don't think he mentioned he was making any alterations until I asked why 1's were cancelling successes). He insisted that it &quot;made characters feel more heroic,&quot; but his adjustment of target numbers and the treatments of ones and tens flattened the bell curve and nudged it to the left. Nor did he put a whole lot of thought into character generation. I took the Dawn--the fighter-type--who only had 6-8 out of 10 Charm selections made, almost all of them out of a single tree, and the others were closely related and redundant (Solar Hero Style up to the form charm along with the first and second Martial Arts Excellency, for those who can make sense of that.)<br /> <br /> The lessons here:<br /> <br /> 1.) What you think is cool <i>is not necessarily cool for everyone</i>. This is really important, and even the good GM's need to know this. Themes, characters, etc. are all good and well, but whether by delivery or by concept, Awesome McCoolpants may not make the table cheer when he shows up, and players may not fall over themselves to fawn over Little Suzie Moedorbs. Repeating yourself and shoving it in our faces DOES NOT MAKE THIS BETTER.<br /> <br /> 2.) Do not ever. EVER. <b><i>EVER</i></b>. damage a character sheet not your own, especially without permission. It's the tangible representation of the character's avatar in the game, and it can represent their involvement and emotional investment like a voodoo doll. Treat it with care<br /> <br /> 3.) Know your player's comfort zones, especially if you're treading into the gray areas that might make people uncomfortable; if you have to wonder if you're coming close to them, you probably are.<br /> <br /> 4.) Convention games can suck. As GM, you need to make sure that multiple characters have some sort of rough concept, a full suite of capabilities, etc, and each one can take a lot longer than you'd like. That said, you volunteered, and the onus is on you to do it right.<br /> <br /> 5.) Rules may not work for you. You may feel inclined to change them. If you're at a convention game, you may attract some new players who aren't familiar with the system--and that's good! Get the word out!--but don't be surprised if at least one of them is going to be confused and/or aggravated by house rules, especially if you aren't 100% clear on them from the get-go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T23:27:12-08:00","id":314280,"title":"","content":"I wasn't going to mention this example until the game ended, but since it has:<br /> <br /> This ST, who I shall call for the sake of convenience Sean, was an amateur film-maker, with all the pretentiousness that implied. He wanted to run a Demon: the Descent game, which I was all in favour of since I liked how it looked. We came up with characters, got the setting read directly, word for word, from the STs notes (in retrospect, that was the first warning), and proceeded to play.<br /> <br /> That game was a solid contender for the second-worst game I've ever played in (I'll share the worst another time). The setting was a liberals political cartoon version of ultra-conservative hillbilly America, with everyone being portrayed as solidly mentally retarded, and so backward that I'm pretty sure the Amish my characters Cover was seemed innovative (ironically I originally intended him to be more old-school than his particular community). He didn't know the rules, which is understandable, but making changes without mentioning them or collaboration with the group is somewhat less so. Included in these changes were: not using the Beat system, ignoring Aspirations, making us roll Subterfuge to lie (for those that don't know, Demons can lie perfectly as an innate ability), and not using the Key/Cipher system, and making the G-M a conceptual entity rather than a physical one. In the opening minutes, one of a characters Followers threw a joint at the character, blowing up a still and the house which was represented by a Merit (Resources, I think, but I can't remember).<br /> <br /> It quickly became apparent that our characters were totally incidental to the story that Sean wanted to tell. The opening thing was that there were people being murdered in really weird way around town. In the one scene we managed to examine, there was a cymbal-monkey that has Aether in it, and a mirror with spatial portal runes around the edge and a stylised mushroom on the back. We could not trace the runes at all, so that was really just a dead-end. In fact, all of our actions never affected the world one iota.<br /> <br /> Then the actual characters started doing stuff. We were seized by an entity who teleported us into an infinite office which we couldn't affect or leave, populated only by a woman we couldn't affect who pontificated pointlessly at us before letting us go. We soon encountered another character, apparently a former character of his, a Mage with, near I can tell, at least 5 points in Space, Life, Matter and Time who was responsible for at least some of the murders. He could and did stop time and wrap one of us up in plastic wrap so deep that the Destroyer with four blade-hands couldn't cut his way out...thrice. He then wanted to cut off the Destroyers feet, and only some quick-thinking by another PC stopped that (god knows we couldn't). He then showed us a described-in-detail entity that was made up of breasts, legs, which Mage guy - again, in exquisite detail - was suckling and grinding against.<br /> <br /> I did try to give constructively-phrased and intended feedback, which he seemed to receive well, even if he didn't act on it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, in an attempt for us to remotely enjoy ourselves, we started giving the nameless characters nicknames. Teleporting office woman was Heisenboobs, Mage was Freudenstein. Eventually Sean got so pissed at our refusal to take the game seriously that he (allegedly) killed the game, and the Meetup page which he was also managing, and stopped booking rooms (we played at a local library). I say allegedly because this was mentioned through an apparently mass e-mail that neither I nor my brother (also a member of the group) got, hours before the group suddenly ceased to exist, in what was possibly the most spectacular tantrum I've been vicarious witness to.<br /> <br /> The whole game was so entirely pointless and unpleasant. He insisted on booking the rooms, but was apparently incapable of doing so. More than half the time the game was held on a different day than expected, with little to no notice. The clearly wanted to tell a story <i>to</i> people, rather than tell a story <i>with</i> people. He not only didn't know the rules of the game, but changed them with no consultation with players, or attention to how they change the game. The setting was cartoonish, the NPCs more like bit characters on the Simpsons rather than what could actually be people, we were totally incidental to the 'plot', and his attempts to draw us into the story were based on just grossing us out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T01:56:24-08:00","id":314335,"title":"","content":"Allan, I guess you've run into some bad luck with STs. I thought your inaugural post of this thread was bad, but I see you have a whole repertoire of stories :/ as amusing they are now, the games weren't so funny I'd guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T03:05:58-08:00","id":314351,"title":"","content":"I always assumed every gamer had had their share of bad STs. Some more than others, of course, but just seems inherent to the nature of the hobby.<br /> <br /> As much as I loathed these STs at the time, if the stories can at least bring someone some chuckles, or improve someones ST-ing, then it can't all be in vain <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T01:45:53-08:00","id":315195,"title":"","content":"I've been playing with the same group since I ever discovered RPG back in 2002. And fortunately, we are four guys: 1 is a good ST, 2 are brilliant STs, and I can't ST even to save my own skin. I'm the ugly duck of the group :P<br /> <br /> The only bad STs I knew were from RPG Meetings that take hold in two cities around here. They are supposed to captivate new players but I guess they do the opposite. Some examples I recall:<br /> <br /> - One ST was doing a VtM session, my friend had a Toreador with dots in Performance which he justified with his character's hobby as Mime. The ST spent 15 minutes asking him why. I was trying to understand what was the problem of someone being a Mime as hobby! Is it strange? Perhaps but so is playing RPG to most people. He finally accepted.<br /> <br /> - Same ST saying the session would take place at some ghost town (metaphorically, there weren't any Wraiths there). Then he asked us why we were there. Well being a one shot game as a demo for new players, everyone did the char on the spot so no backgrounds besides one or two lines. Then he got mad because no one had a plausible explanation to be a vampire in a god forsaken town -.-' &quot;Dude, it's your story, you're the ST, you prepared the session. How about ignoring that or come prepared next time?&quot;.<br /> <br /> - Other ST started disallowing every rule that favoured the PCs and enforcing to the full extent of the rule all that made the PCs life harder.<br /> <br /> - Another ST was a rules freak, everything was done by the book with figurines and calculators whenever needed. Boring session as hell where the RP aspect was completely killed.<br /> <br /> And this is why I stopped going to RPG Meetings. Although I had loads of fun in one playing OG <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2435-prophet","name":"Prophet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2435_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"329"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-23T06:49:23-08:00","id":348239,"title":"","content":"There have to be more bad ST stories out there. Maybe I should create a &quot;Praising ST&quot; thread, balance things out?<br /> <br /> This story is kind of an odd one. I was introduced to Exalted through this group I still play with, and this guy, who I shall name Adam, ran a game where we were Solar, nominally part of a mercenary company in Nexus, but we mostly did our own thing, and he did a great job of incorporating our goals and making us feel relevant. Even my character, who was a bit vague to be honest, but he did a really good job. I thoroughly enjoyed that game, and still rate it as one of the best games I've played in.<br /> <br /> So that game inevitably finished, and we moved onto other games. A while later, he asked if we wanted to come back to the setting. The way things worked out, most of us ended up with new characters, but I didn't mind too much. This game... was not good, at least in my opinion. A lot of other people seemed to be enjoying themselves, so I want to stress that this could just be me.<br /> <br /> The game mostly revolved around dealing with the Primordial that was released at the end of the first game (it sounds terrible, but it really worked as a climax), and our new characters were resisting it. The game started strong, although there were a couple bumps, but nothing terrible. Then we met up with the other Exalted who were fighting the Primordial, and the primary flaw of the game started to show itself. Now, it's inevitable in that context that something of the players characters will lose something of their special-ness, I get that. But every Exalt apart from us had a 300+ experience, and perfect knowledge of the fluff as well as the STs executive decision about what was &quot;right&quot;. One Twilight character, for example, was played by a player whose knowledge of the books was largely limited to the core and Manuals of Exalted Power. If it wasn't in one of those, he didn't know it. But when he contested the NPCs idea of how X worked due to what seemed to me to be totally valid reasoning, he was called stupid and useless IC, with the ST OOC saying that it is clearly spelt out how X works in &quot;one of the books&quot;. This was consistent: NPCs were always correct, and disagreeing with them therefore indicated that our characters didn't know what we were talking about.<br /> <br /> This NPC-driven nature of the story was continued, and in fact got worse. No matter what our specialty was, if we disagreed with direction taken by the NPC of our area, we were &quot;shown to be wrong&quot;. A Warleader-type Solar was set up in opposition to a Manipulator, who employed and worked with the Solar who was responsible for unleashing the Primordial in the first place. The Manipulator, who had a Sorcerer working for him, apparently had at least 5 points in all Twilight Abilities, plus 3 dot specialities in everything, plus Solar-level sorcery, plus god knows what. Basically, if he wanted to do it, he could with trivial effort, which put both the sorcery-focussed and magitech-focussed PCs right into the redundant pile, which he did, a lot. The Manipulator, who was the biggest offender, not only knew about the Great Curse and <i>everything including the ins and outs of the Ebon Dragons plans</i> and expected everyone to just believe him (which of course all NPCs did, and any PC that didn't was treated as paranoid or stupid), also had 3 Exaltations of different kinds somehow, and all his plans always worked out, no matter how many assumptions were built into them.<br /> <br /> In short (shorter, at least) we were not at all relevant. We either went along with the NPCs, in which case we weren't relevant because there were more skilled NPCs already doing the stuff we should do, or we didn't, in which case we were outside the expected plotline and nothing we did ever came to anything. I found this particularly annoying, because I was playing a sorcery character who the ST had described as &quot;probably the best sorcerer in Creation&quot;; he was my old character who I later picked up again, and had spent the last 4 to 5 years improving his Solar Sorcery. Not that you'd know it, because sorcery was treated as totally useless. Shadowland closing? There were like 3 in Creation, and all in enemy territory. Creatures of Darkness hurting? Pfft, drop one combat NPC into the area, or the CoD had some way of shielding themselves. I even considered researching the spell to withdraw someones soul, to deal with the Warlord who, in Adams words rolled &quot;all the dice in the house, and got even more automatic successes&quot;. Adam said it wouldn't work; not because he was an Exalt, but because it would take too long to research, and the Sidereals, who up to this point had been basically the running excuse for how the Manipulator knew literally everything, suddenly decided to not be helpful to my character because his support of the Manipulator, who had hired the releaser of the Primordial, I remind you, was qualified. Adam also said that it wouldn't work anyway; he was of the opinion sorcery was useless, and he was enforcing this view just as hard as he could without actually breaking the written rules. This was after I had gone through two characters, with one dying due to not having a surprise negator in the stand-up fight that wasn't supposed to happen in the sneaking mission (playing a non-combat-focussed Infernal: they don't have as easy access to surprise negators at best), and me choosing to abandon another due to being totally irrelevant.<br /> <br /> The game was awful. If it had gone on any longer, I would have pulled out. I wasn't enjoying it, I wasn't relevant to the story, the story was fine (just don't pretend you're going to affect it one jot). I pointed this out to Adam several times, and he always acted like it was my fault. I have no idea what happened; his first game was great! This one though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:02:50-08:00","id":367141,"title":"","content":".An <a href=\"http://irolledazero.blogspot.com.au/2013/04/the-sue-system-rise-of-marty.html\" target=\"_blank\">ST analogue</a> to the <a href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/rpg/michelle/\" target=\"_blank\">Michelle Chronicles</a>, submitted for your reading, enjoyment, and hopefully, learning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T08:54:50-08:00","id":384261,"title":"","content":"So, this one's a bit different : it took place in a larp. A French Larp in fact, which I'm told is the equivalent of an &quot;hardcore larp&quot; in the US.<br /> <br /> It was inspired from the Warhammer universe : the story took place before the corebooks, we were playing during the early years of the empire. In fact, Sigmar only became a god during the last larp. The story was fine, and so did the players. My character's backstory was a blast : I trusted the head ST to write it, and I had the pleasure of discovering that I got the role of the eldest son of the emperor, but not his heir, since I was also a mage, which means that I was officialy banned from any position of power (but by exploiting a bunch of loopholes, I quickly got a siege in the noble assembly).<br /> <br /> Anyway : long story short, we find my father dying from a wound that looks magically incurable. After much heated debate between players about who will be the next emperor, we learn that almost all of the main Lords in the empire (basically, those who ruled each tribe) had been murdered by the Queen of the Asobornes, an amazon-like tribe., thanks to various corrupted artifacts, and she planed on marching on us next (we were in a secluded refuge for my brother's birthday, which meant that many high officers of the realm were here, including me). So, we scrambled for a solution, and some players actually have the idea of calling her former lover for help : a champion gladiator and former slave. And who's playing this role? The head ST.<br /> So, we got treated to a scene between the Queen and her paramour, where we could literaly do nothing but watch. In fact, when most of us yelled insults at the queen (understable since, you know, she <i>killed our leaders</i>), the slave got pissed off and berated us for behaving like dumb peasants and interrupting his love talk with her. He even threatened us to strike down the next one who would speak up.<br /> And of course, I did. After she mocked us one last time, I yelled that she was just a corrupted puppet. And thus, the ST came toward me, swords drawn, and struck me down. I stood my ground, since I'm a mage, I didn't know how to fight in a duel and, oh, I don't know, I thought it felt right to insult my parents' assassin?!<br /> My friends managed to heal me, with the help of a priest of death and a priest of life, but then the scene was over : basically, it was a cinematic, and we couldn't interact with it. But a few hours later, while I was helping with a ritual, the St came to see me and asked me why I wasn't dead : I explained to him that I got healed quickly, and he got mad, saying that I should have been dead the moment he hit me, and that I did a mistake. However, it was too late, and I was too much involved in the story to correct this, so he just stormed off mad.<br /> <br /> And that's just the most glaring example of this larp's problem : the ST was an attention whore. basically, when he had to play a NPC, we were supposed to stand back and watch as he performed. And his story was planned from the beginning, with no hope of deviating it, we had to endure it. The monsters were WAY too strong, despite the fact that we were supposed to be badass : we were 5 mages, and we supposedly had huge powers that could kill one-shot people at a huge cost. <i>Except that it didn't work on the most basic of orks.</i> So, we were forced to retreat and resist until a convenient squadron of super-rangers led by, you guessed it, the same ST, saved the day. AGAIN.<br /> <br /> Worst part of it? When I went to talk to him afterwards, I couldn't even have the chance to say my feelings. He greeted me with sarcasm, jokingly calling me a cheater for my &quot;stupid death-defying stunt&quot;.<br /> <br /> Woaw. It sure feels good to rant!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T14:19:05-08:00","id":394107,"title":"","content":"Man, bad ST's. I think we had them all.<br /> <br /> I recently was in a Pathfinder Game, which I quit. I lived in a small town and we only had 2 STs in the whole area. I could not get a game off the ground because no one knew me. So you had ST 1 who was really bad or ST 2 who liked to kill off everyone. In fact he got a sick joy in it. Going out of his way killing our characters. He especially liked killing one of the player's characters every week until the point we joked about the player needing a character-o-matic. I got sick of this and talked to the ST, who then told one of the other players who I did not even talk about, I had issues with that player. I quit. Got a Mage the Ascension game off the ground for people who ended up enjoying it. <br /> <br /> I was in a VTM game where we were all recently presented to the Prince and the Prince told us we had 3 weeks to show our loyalty to him. Well we all were like crap what we do? Well one of the players did not show up for 2 games and missed the first game so his character was not presented to the Prince. So he comes in as character, he wants to help us with our mission from the Prince to show loyalty and maybe the Prince will let him live... so we all talked about it and planned to knock the character out and present this character to the Prince. After all this Lick was not at his Presentation and the Prince had called a Blood Hunt on the SoB. ST would not let us because he said it would break the Traditions and he did not want to see his friend backstabbed like that... <br /> We all quit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4949-nene-richards","name":"Nene Richards","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4949_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T09:13:46-08:00","id":398805,"title":"","content":"I have been fairly lucky. The worst I can say isn't that I've had &quot;bad&quot; STs so much as &quot;boring&quot; ones for the games I've ended up not liking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2058-nobody","name":"Nobody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:54:23-07:00","id":928403,"title":"","content":"Most of my bad STs have been bad GMs -- D&amp;D, specifically. For Exalted, only a few examples stand out and they still aren't nearly as bad as the D&amp;D examples [which is sad to think on].<br /> <br /> A Dragon-Blooded ST who operated from the presumption that DBs were incapable of doing anything not explicitly defined by their charms, since they weren't Solars. Basic capabilities were completely irrelevant, efforts to progress the plot were stymied, and the Solaroid NPCs who showed up were more important than the PCs.<br /> <br /> A ST who basically refused to actually cooperate with efforts, disguised as obliviousness. Attempting to ply desires from mortal NPCs for a chance to use Cecelynian wish charms failed because he was just blithely &quot;yay someone is talking ot my NPCs I am good ST&quot;. Game ended mercifully fast.<br /> <br /> Another ST did the More Important Than You NPC parade thing. Asked for what actions everyone was doing in downtime, then made them basically irrelevant footnotes in a setting document next to all the glorious escapades of her NPCs all based on former PCs. I changed my character after a few sessions early on, having realized that interacting with any NPC with a name was a doomed endeavor because she didn't want them to be affected by PCs in any way. And then she unilaterally decided we were abandoning the Exalted system and changing over to Nobilis. Predictably the game did not continue.<br /> <br /> I might have had bad WoD STs? I don't recall stuff that was specifically STs and not just my not liking WoD conceits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 07-08-2016, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:29:12-07:00","id":928425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=290487#post290487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Biggest gripe I ever had with an ST was in a LARP where he let his girlfriend have a bunch of extra points at character creation, so she was a 7th gen Toreador right out of the gate. After they broke up, it turned ugly for her. I set her up as the prime suspect in my character's destruction and other people in the game (who didn't like her either) smelled the blood in the water and got her Diableriezed WITH THE PRINCE'S SANCTION by the Tremere.<br /> <br /> Besides that, not had a lot of complaints, but I've also spent a lot of time AS the ST, so it's a little different for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why i am loath to play in games where the DM/GM/ST has a significant other (wife, husband, boy/girl friend) cause all too often i have seen it get to where said S.O is shown favoritism..<br /> <br /> YES i have met some hubby/wife combos that didn't do that, and many others say that they don't, but if you watch them gaming often enough, you can still spot the unconscious favoritism showing up.<br /> <br /> And as to the most often ST side of house that is me to a tee.. I'd say in the past decade of my gaming, i have spent a solid 70 to 75% of the time Running games..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=290529#post290529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ALMOST dead but never kills us. I do not mind having my characters die, but he refuses to kill us.</div> </div> </div> </div>These sorts of gms, who are so scared to ever kill a player's character, cause they feel they might get too much aggro from said players, and they don't like dealing with conflict, are almost as bad as the DM/GM who LOVES just killing pcs and gloats about it..<br /> <br /> <br /> Now for me, the 2 most bad ST/GM/DM's i have played under was one for an ADND 1e game and a dm for a Star wars D6 game. Both had the same mindset, to where players/PCs were the heroes in HIS film and as such HE just HAD to ensure they always had plot immunity just like any film maker does for his mainline characters, to the point that even though he always rolled in the open (the ADND dm HATED and loathed DM screens, while the SW dm just played on couches and chairs so just rolled in a small box on a coffee table), but would always ignore the rolls if it EVER would lead to any sort of failure for the players. <br /> <br /> The first one (The SW game master) i ONLY played that one game with him. Even when i saw him several years later, i refused to sit down with his group..The other one, i actually lured 4 of his 7 die hard players away to form my own group...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:50:30-07:00","id":929453,"title":"","content":"A little wisdom I've picked up over the years which I call The Rule of Vader.<br /> <br /> The Rule of Vader stipulates that if the GM of a game set in a pre-existing universe includes a big-name villain, the party will drop whatever it is doing and put all of its efforts into killing the bad guy, utterly derailing the plot.<br /> <br /> Named after Darth Vader, whose inclusion into your Star Wars game will guarantee that the party will move heaven and earth in an attempt to kill him. If they're smart they'll not run at him brandishing their weapons. If they aren't that smart... well, TPK awaits. And if they do kill him the story that the GM has written will be so utterly derailed a new one needs to be written up.<br /> <br /> A variant would be The Rule of Caine, which is when the party cannot actually kill the person in question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T02:38:53-07:00","id":930254,"title":"","content":"Well, I've had a few bad ones but the the absolute worst was when I started playing RPGs with DnD. I was about 13 and admittedly I wasn't a great player, my first character was one of those horrible bully Paladins, but I digress. I learned early on the best thing was to always play male characters since everyone always flirted with female ones but this DM just wouldn't let it slide. As soon as I made a male character he'd die right out of the gate, and the DM would suggest I make a female one. So I made a female Half-Orc and I even printed off a picture of the most scarred up and old female half-orc I could find. When she died, I made a married character but that just started flirtations about how she was doomed to cheat. I really didn't get it at the time, and kinda viewed it as a game of how much I could still follow his &quot;rules&quot; while making it difficult (some of which became off kilter NPCs when I learned to DM). The owners banned him from the store when they caught him trying to feel up another girl who was even younger than I was. It is really creepy in hindsight, but I just remember being really frustrated that he wouldn't let any of my characters live and being gleeful about the different ways I tried to stump him. The full creep factor didn't hit me until I was an adult.<br /> <br /> One game I played had a setting with deep polarizing political issues as part of the setting and we all talked about this and decided how our group leaned, but the GM felt strongly about the other side and within the first few minutes of the game told us that if we fought his NPC we would die. Turned out he made a level 20 character when the rules hadn't even come out yet. The game only had rules up to level 5. Not only did he force us to act a particular way but he bent the lore of the world to glorify his own character and previous characters he'd made, often making NPCs change important political stances to glorify him and then insult us with the opposite view. He used the game to preach politics, not even real issues but ones solely found in the game. One of the few games I ever walked out of.<br /> <br /> We revolve around STs to protect against burnout, so it really isn't his fault, but one of the other players enjoys running games but they almost always end in us intentionally/unintentionally getting ourselves killed. He sets up whole plots with defined sequence of events. If we don't know what to do, nothing happens. He gets annoyed when we don't like the NPCs he has scripted into allying with us and it becomes a long slog of poking things until he reveals the exact action we need to progress the plot. It's a grind. One player refused to go to the hospital after getting hurt because that was the one thing he could control. Eventually we try to hide our hit points from him so he will accidentally kill us, and eventually pick on the big bad directly in what we know is a suicidal attempt. It's hard because he is new and the only way to get better is practice, but it's grueling and a slog to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T05:30:04-07:00","id":930287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=930254#post930254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As soon as I made a male character he'd die right out of the gate, and the DM would suggest I make a female one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like you said, you were 13 back then but when your DM pulls stuff like that on you you know it's time to pack up and leave the game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12085-beriorn","name":"Beriorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12085_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T06:17:02-07:00","id":930296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beriorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=930287#post930287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like you said, you were 13 back then but when your DM pulls stuff like that on you you know it's time to pack up and leave the game</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it's obvious now, but back then it was my first real hobby and I took it as hazing the young kid. Most of the DMs didn't really change their tone if kids joined their games, but after that the owners got a game together that they personally DMed for the rest of us. We kept that game going til graduation. We even threw something special when prom hit to give each of us a bit of a send off, so it worked out. There's unlikely to ever be a thread for Wonderful STs but I always felt those two deserved it; especially looking back on some of the crazy antics we put them through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T15:14:46-07:00","id":930542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>3Comrades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/290174-bitching-about-st-thread?p=930296#post930296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's unlikely to ever be a thread for Wonderful STs but I always felt those two deserved it; especially looking back on some of the crazy antics we put them through.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/348279-praising-sts\">There is</a>, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 07-12-2016, 10:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T07:57:40-07:00","id":983921,"title":"","content":"I was once in a shadowrun game where ST killed off my character by making my character do things I never said he did. I played a decker that had a negative quality where he would get angry like people do on xbox and talk big but never did anything. The GM decided no your character does do what he says and because of it a force 12 spirit of air shows up at my characters house. My character is level living a high living area with extra security and he says the spirit showed up when all the security went on a coffee break. Then he had the spirit carry me to a where house that when it took me in I did not get any rolls to escape he just said it blows up and you died. So I said ok....can I burn an edge to survive. He said yes but no one finds you in the rubble and you bleed out and die. <br /> <br /> I had another GM that got angry at the whole group when he set up a job that he meant to be really hard but one of the players found a simple way around the whole job and rather then the job taking 3 games like he said it should it took us 2 hours to finish. So he quit the game and cursed us all out. <br /> <br /> I had another gm who ran world of darkness who would fall a sleep while running not once but every game. Then he would leave for not just 1 hour but 3 hours at a time. When he was gone he would leave his TV playing super loud in the background. He got mad when a bunch of players left. One time he was gone so long a player started to GM in his place and when the real GM got back he kicked that guy out the group for trying to steal players. Oh and once in his game I did 33 agg to another character and he said I did zero damage because the person is important to the plot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}